<p>
  This Privacy Policy explains how <strong>ONYX</strong> (“ONYX”, “we”, “us”),
  operated by <span class="legal__ph">[your registered business / proprietor name]</span>,
  <span class="legal__ph">[registered address, City, State, India]</span>, collects and
  uses your personal data when you visit this website or contact us. We act as the
  <strong>Data Fiduciary</strong> for this data under India’s
  <strong>Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023 (DPDP Act)</strong>.
</p>

<h2>1. What we collect</h2>
<p>We only collect what we need to respond to you and run this site:</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Information you give us</strong> via the contact form — your name and email
    (required), and optionally company, website, phone, service interest, budget and your
    message. You provide this voluntarily when you choose to contact us.</li>
  <li><strong>Basic technical data</strong> your browser sends to our hosting provider
    (such as IP address and request logs) for security and to keep the site running. We do
    not use this to build a profile of you.</li>
  <li><strong>Local browser storage</strong> for essential preferences only (your cookie
    choice and whether you’ve seen the intro). See our
    <a href="/cookies">Cookies Policy</a>.</li>
</ul>
<p>We do <strong>not</strong> run advertising trackers, analytics pixels, or sell your data.</p>

<h2>2. Why we use it (purpose)</h2>
<ul>
  <li>To reply to your enquiry and provide the services you ask about.</li>
  <li>To keep records of our communications and any agreement we enter into.</li>
  <li>To secure, operate and improve the website.</li>
</ul>
<p>Our legal basis is your <strong>consent</strong> (given when you submit the form) and,
  where relevant, the steps needed to enter into or perform a contract with you.</p>

<h2>3. How long we keep it</h2>
<p>We keep contact enquiries only as long as needed to respond and for our legitimate
  business records, and then delete them. You can ask us to delete your data sooner (see
  “Your rights”).</p>

<h2>4. Who we share it with</h2>
<p>We do not sell your personal data. We share it only with service providers that help us
  operate — for example our website host and email provider — and only so they can perform
  that service for us. These are:</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Hosting / infrastructure:</strong> <span class="legal__ph">[your host, e.g. Vercel / Render / AWS]</span></li>
  <li><strong>Fonts:</strong> Google Fonts (may receive your IP when the page loads fonts).</li>
  <li><strong>Content delivery (CDN):</strong> cdnjs / jsDelivr (serve script libraries).</li>
</ul>

<h2>5. Your rights under the DPDP Act</h2>
<p>As a Data Principal, you have the right to:</p>
<ul>
  <li>Access a summary of the personal data we hold about you and how we process it.</li>
  <li>Ask us to correct, complete, update or erase your personal data.</li>
  <li>Withdraw your consent at any time (this won’t affect processing already done).</li>
  <li>Nominate another person to exercise your rights in case of death or incapacity.</li>
  <li>Raise a grievance with us, and escalate to the Data Protection Board of India.</li>
</ul>
<p>To exercise any of these, email us at <a href="mailto:<%= site.email %>"><%= site.email %></a>.</p>

<h2>6. Grievance Officer</h2>
<p>
  If you have concerns about how we handle your data, contact our Grievance Officer:<br />
  <span class="legal__ph">[Grievance Officer name]</span> — <a href="mailto:<%= site.email %>"><%= site.email %></a>.
  We will acknowledge and respond within the timelines required by law.
</p>

<h2>7. Children</h2>
<p>This site is not directed at children under 18. We do not knowingly collect the personal
  data of a child without verifiable parental/guardian consent, as required by the DPDP Act.
  If you believe a child has given us data, contact us and we will delete it.</p>

<h2>8. Security</h2>
<p>We apply reasonable technical and organisational measures to protect your data. No method
  of transmission or storage is completely secure, but we work to safeguard the information
  you share with us and will notify affected users and the Board of a reportable breach as
  required.</p>

<h2>9. Changes</h2>
<p>We may update this policy as our practices or the law change. The “last updated” date at
  the top reflects the latest version.</p>
